"comparison":"Both NVIDIA and Intel explicitly address climate impacts and environmental sustainability as part of their business strategy and risk assessment. NVIDIA states it 'addresses our climate impacts across our product lifecycle and assesses risks, including current and emerging regulations and market impacts.' Similarly, Intel details its environmental strategies, noting that it 'builds energy efficiency into our products to help our customers lower their own emissions' and 'focuses on addressing climate change impacts upstream and downstream in the value chain.' Both companies frame climate action within the context of product lifecycle management and regulatory/market risk assessment, though Intel provides more specific detail on emissions reduction and customer energy usage benefits.",
